data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"With grand mean `m`, `SSB = Σ n_i (m_i − m)²` and `SSW = Σ (x − m_i)²`. Use `df1 = k − 1` and\n`df2 = N − k`. Then `F = (SSB / df1) / (SSW / df2)`, and `p` is the upper tail of the F distribution with\nthose two degrees of freedom. `scipy.stats.f.sf` gives that tail."},"hints_note":null}

